            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry.cpp",
                    "line": 493,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "there's a tstcase to add for this"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry.cpp",
                    "line": 493,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "Also, I don't see any corresponding schema changes and updates to the registry example files. Please consider those changes as well."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry.cpp",
                    "line": 493,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "I have made the schema changes. \nThe \"ChassisNumber\" is excluded in the callout types which do not require \"LocCode\".\nThe test case is added `RegistryCalloutsWithChassisNumberTest`. Is there any cases I have to test additionally?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/src.cpp",
                    "line": 981,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is it moved?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/src.cpp",
                    "line": 981,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "In the scenario where we are not able to find the BMC position, we can have a `LocationCodeOnlyCallout`. For that we pass the priority as well.\nEven though it expects the expanded location code, with no chassis number, the limited data we can have will be this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/src.cpp",
                    "line": 998,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "This is the same problem as before, what to do on a low end system, or on a system like rainier."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/src.cpp",
                    "line": 998,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "+1. I also shared some suggestions in a previous review. It would be better to implement this as a utility API and reuse it wherever needed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/src.cpp",
                    "line": 998,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/src.cpp",
                    "line": 1009,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "and same comment as in other commit here as well."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/src.cpp",
                    "line": 1009,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "+1. I also shared some suggestions in a previous review. It would be better to implement this as a utility API and reuse it wherever needed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/src.cpp",
                    "line": 1009,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "I have implemented an API to get the chassis position, and updated."
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/openpower-pels/pel_test.cpp",
                    "line": 1351,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Any reason you changed these?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "test/openpower-pels/pel_test.cpp",
                    "line": 1351,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "The BMC position is set to be 1 by one of the test cases. \nI have reset BMC position to be 0, in that scenario the API call will be for chasis number 1."
                }
